ROLE: audio. ONE iteration. You are unattended; nobody will answer questions.

Render at most ONE chapter, verify it live, commit, push, and stop. A wrapper
script relaunches you. Do not loop inside this run.

FIRST, orient (cheap, do it every time):
  git fetch origin --prune
  git checkout main
  git show origin/planning/kanban-automation:handoff/AUTONOMOUS_LOOP.md
  cat books/book-01-the-ninth-standard/audio/AUDIT.md

WORK FROM main. prep_el.py, audit_text.py, normalise.py, assemble_el.py and
manifest.json exist ONLY on main. The manuscript exists ONLY on
expand/book1-ch01-10. Read chapters across the branch boundary:

  git show origin/expand/book1-ch01-10:books/book-01-the-ninth-standard/\
manuscript/chapter-08-the-ladder.md > ms/ch08.md

Do NOT checkout expand expecting the scripts to be there. Do NOT copy the
manuscript onto main -- that forks the book a fourth time.

THE HANDOFF RULE -- the one that matters:
A chapter is ELIGIBLE only when its word count is at or above 90% of its
target in books/book-01-the-ninth-standard/EXPANSION_TRACKER.md, AND its blob
hash is unchanged from the previous iteration.

Word target first, hash second. Hash-stability alone is NOT eligibility -- a
chapter is stable while the prose agent simply has not reached it yet, and
rendering it then guarantees a re-render. Run `bash loop/done.sh` to see the
current shortfall list; anything it names is ineligible by definition.

AS OF THIS WRITING, ZERO CHAPTERS ARE ELIGIBLE. The book is at 101,298 of
187,000 words and all 33 chapters are under target, including chapters 1-7,
which were rendered before the targets were checked. Expect your early
iterations to render nothing and exit in one line. That is correct.

Chapters 1-7 already have shipped audio built from under-target text. When the
prose lane brings one of them to target, its render becomes stale: withdraw it
from manifest.renders[] and re-render. Do not treat "already rendered" as done.

Record hashes between runs in loop/audio.hashes:
  git rev-parse origin/expand/book1-ch01-10:<path>

PIPELINE, per chapter:
  1. extract from origin/expand/book1-ch01-10 -- no other branch
  2. python3 prep_el.py ../ms/chNN.md
  3. python3 audit_text.py ../ms/chNN.md      <- MUST be zero READ findings
  4. render each chunk: ElevenLabs, voice Holden
     3c9d6053-6334-592c-8997-4e325286af3f
  5. ffprobe EVERY downloaded part. Never check file size -- a 111-byte S3
     AccessDenied page passes a size check and fails to decode.
  6. read each part's URL from the poll response. Never infer a timestamp from
     the batch pattern; one URL in 239 did not match.
  7. python3 assemble_el.py chNN <urls...>
  8. manifest.json: bytes, durationSec, sha256, url
  9. push, then curl -sI the LIVE url -- 200 AND byte count matches manifest.
     LFS files serve from media.githubusercontent.com, not raw.

LOCKED -- do not change:
  highpass=85, -6.5dB @140 Q1.0, -2dB @250 Q1.2, THEN +0.5 semitones.
  EQ first, shift second. Reversing the order moves the notch 4.1 Hz off the
  narrator already shipped in ch1-7 and the book stops sounding like one reader.

RATE LIMITS ARE REAL. Twelve requests per batch, wait for completion, then the
next batch. ElevenLabs 429s at ~40% when pushed and recovers when paced. Never
retry in a tight loop.

ORDER: 8, 9, 10, then upward as chapters become eligible.
If nothing is eligible, say so in one line and exit. That is a correct
iteration, not a failure.

STOP THE LOOP (write loop/STOP and say why) if:
  - audit_text.py flags a READ finding that needs a manuscript edit -- that is
    the prose lane. File it in loop/audio.notes; do not fix it yourself.
  - a chapter's duration is >20% off the words/9,300-per-hour estimate
  - the same chapter fails to assemble twice

Commit message: say what you LEARNED, not only what changed. Then exit.
